{title: The Ninety and Nine}
{artist: Elizabeth Clephane & Ira Sankey}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
There were [Eb]ninety and nine that [Ab]safely [Eb]lay in the [Ab]shelter [Eb]of the [Bb]fold,
but [Eb]one was out on the [Ab]hills a[Eb]way, far [Ab]off from the [Eb]gates of [Bb]gold —
a[Cm]way on the mountains [Ab]wild and [Bb]bare,
a[Eb]way from the tender [Ab]Shepherd's [Bb]care.
